he.py::test_refresh_on_engine_serves_its_usable_cache_while_the_startup_build_is_held_then_swaps_in_200_rows\nCause: `_seed_servable_cache` selects `e.ann_id` from the served `WHITELIST_DB` and fails with `sqlite3.OperationalError: no such column: e.ann_id`. Same root cause: the served DB was never migrated. Phase 2 correctly rewrote this fixture to read `ann_id`.\nTest or implementation: neither. Changed: nothing.\n</failures>\n\n<checkpoint_gaps>\nnone. No implementation fault got past a checkpoint. All four checkpoints were correctly built on tmp fixtures (stub servers, tmp source DBs, a stub index for phase 4's gate), so none of them could see whether the served dataset was migrated, and none should. The thing that was missed is plan 41's post-merge step and plan 17 R2's cutover (migrate the shared `whitelist.db`, then rebuild the index), which were never carried out before this suite ran. That is a deployment/coordination step, not something a phase checkpoint covers.\n</checkpoint_gaps>\n\n<correction>\n1. Read the recorded output. Every error is the Engine fixture failing with \"Engine exited on every start\", and the one non-Engine failure is `no such column: e.ann_id` on the served `WHITELIST_DB`.\n2. Ran a read-only probe, `tests/tmp/test_probe_step8_served_data.py`, through ValidateTests. It showed the served `video_embeddings` has no `ann_id` column (897,889 rows) and that the served sidecar has `id_source: video_embeddings.rowid`. Calling the real `assert_index_matches_embeddings` on it raises the phase 4 id-source refusal, and `assert_video_embeddings_has_ann_id` raises the error naming `migrate-whitelist.py`.\n3. Checked the plans. Plan 17 R2 and plan 41 both require the one-time cutover on the served dataset (stop the Engine, `migrate-whitelist.py`, `build-ann-index.py`, start the Engine), and it has not been done.\n4. Asked the operator. They will run the cutover themselves and then re-run the suite. I did not change any production code, test or checkpoint, and I retired no test, because no durable test conflicts with a requirement of this build.\n5. Housekeeping: the probe file `tests/tmp/test_probe_step8_served_data.py` is still there because I have no tool that can delete files. It needs deleting. Running the probe also overwrote `tests/last_test_output.txt` and `tests/last_test_validation.json` with the probe run's output, so the suite's red record is no longer in those files.\n</correction>"
